  "body": "When expanding/collapsing the `<details>` element, it's really easy to select the text in the `<summary>` element accidentally when expanding and collapsing a section quickly (just for a quick short look at the section, for example), which is annoying.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I'd like to see the selection of the `<summary>` element disabled by default, but I'm also glad to hear other people's comments on this suggestion.\r\n\r\nBugs in browsers:\r\n\r\n* [Firefox](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1413897)\r\n* [Chromium](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=780811)",
